    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1574">

                <pb facs="1002" n="886" xml:id="pg886"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.62/44.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Special Agent
                        Carothers.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 14, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The German Ambassador called to-day at the Department and made inquiry as to
                    treatment which might be expected for German subjects at Torreon. Ask Villa for
                    proper assurances on this matter which may be communicated to the
                    Ambassador.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
